    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d374">

                <pb facs="0513" n="409" sameAs="frus:frus1913/pg409"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 837.911/18.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the American Minister.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1913-02-20">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 20, 1913</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The following aide mémoire has been handed to the Cuban Minister, who has also
                    had the views of the Department brought to his attention: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p rendition="#center">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">The Department of State to the Cuban
                                Legation.</hi>
                        </p>
                        <p rendition="#center">
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">aide mémoire.</hi>
                        </p>
                        <p>From reports received from the American Minister at Habana the Government
                            of the United States notes with surprise that the Government of Cuba
                            seems to be displaying apathy in the prosecution of those persons
                            responsible for the recent scurrilous newspaper attacks on the personnel
                            of the Legation.</p>
                        <p>It is with regret that the Government of the United States finds itself
                            obliged to direct the attention of the Government of Cuba to this matter
                            and to insist that the persons guilty of those attacks be adequately and
                            speedily dealt with.</p>
                        <p>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington, February 20, 1913.</hi>
                        </p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Knox</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
